# Amendment 1.0.2: split RR08 without weakening the parent repair

RR08's reviewed donor `f0389bb7360bfa6246e66fe92144cb4b4eaa6269` changes 378 added plus 100 deleted handwritten production lines: 478 changed lines exceed the ordinary 400-line cap. This amendment adds RR08a and RR08b rather than granting a budget exception. Each child retains 400 changed production and 900 authored lines. Count additions and deletions after ordinary formatting; estimates do not authorize execution above either cap.

RR08a admits selected copied values before reservation: copied_text/copied_datum, kind allocation, references and merge preparation. It retains the existing whole-State snapshot transaction and its known growth limitations. Merge copies and charges every source field before discarding shadowed fields, including target-array Datum copying; it does not copy only retained entries. The estimated delta is 146 added/20 deleted = 166 changed production lines; two preserved original regressions and the permitted construction.rs work expectation adjustment give a conservative 363-line combined source/test estimate.

RR08b replaces snapshots with the complete undo journal across every transactional mutator, nested rollback and atomic publication, then charges repeated finish containment labels. Do not remove snapshots before allocation, fields, frames, kind, action, merge and CST effects all journal correctly. Its estimate is 243 added/91 deleted = 334 changed production lines, with a conservative 631-line combined source/test estimate. Restore the complete 486-line original regression file (SHA-256 `2d80e2449b9424f715925e80c250f0f5633ee0130ba9a2bd97563ea0b37bcb8d`).

These are conservative source-only SequenceMatcher estimates from actual method regions, not executed child results or authoritative future Git counts. Intermediate merge adaptation causes turnover between children. The final reviewed donor kernel is 968 lines, SHA-256 `0a3b7c3a13b4951d059fa1f446d65c56cda99cae5b6c0cfa6ee08c4cbf77baf9`; differences require an independently reviewed disposition. Detailed regions, cases and estimate methods are retained in the child lane records and source audit `/workspace/build/builderbob/syson-batch21-20261029/rr08-next-admission-audit.json`, SHA-256 `b70fc163fbfb4cde1e6f5f5fdc5835c612cb07b1629c631b06792aa71282ff27`.

RR08a precedes RR08b; RR08b precedes parent integration. Both children modify the same AST kernel/test paths and require sequential exclusive leases with explicit handoff. Root alone owns manifests, locks, exports and the inherited construction.rs max_work3->17 adjustment, without weakening spent-ID assertions. Actual current F11/F12 prerequisite admission and caller wiring remain mandatory. Original PR references 11/41 retain provenance and obligations; use a reviewed current-main extraction rather than replacing current F11 with an obsolete crate snapshot. No new full P14, F13/F14 acceptance or held graph dependency is introduced.

RR08 retains its original task, verification, budget, finding and owner units. Its original kernel/test write authority is explicitly delegated to the two children; the parent authors integration/evidence under its original RR08 evidence directory. Parent acceptance requires both children and the complete combined repair. Its existing downstream consumer edges remain unchanged.

All nine original RR08 regressions, all 37 AST and 27 adapter cases, all 15 current F11 cases and all 12 original F12 cases remain required. Measure actual 100/1000/5000-node construction and F12 postprocessing separately. Exercise real parser construction, nested success/failure, cancellation, refusal before large reservation, foreign handles, CST restoration, spent IDs, partial defaults/adopted kinds and repeated finish labels. Preserve original failures and qualify exact final sources and actual callers independently.

Use release measurements with identical setup outside the timer, two warmups plus seven measured repetitions and raw min/median/max. Keep latency, allocation traffic, live/retained memory and RSS/HWM separate. A seven-sample range is not p95. Preserve the known 79 empty-$children comparison differences and 172 OPEN items assigned to existing families; investigate any additional required finite mismatch. Neither child qualification nor parent structural qualification establishes full native/cache/reference/CST lifecycle, parser/application/capacity acceptance or release closure.

The contract now assigns 780 review units: the original 778 plus two children. Preserve every original obligation except the explicit reviewed RR08 source-authority delegation and scheduling expansion, all 55 historical execution-unit objects and prior integration history. Historical receipts and amendment 1.0.1 retain their original identities; current bindings move to 1.0.2. Future legitimate ledger progress remains possible. F10/F11 remain the only legacy budget dispositions. Every owner hold and performance policy remains in force.

The machine contract binds this note and the split policy. Static checks reject missing children, changed caps/counting, dropped original IDs or parent obligations, detached child acceptance, reordered shared writers and missing whole-parent gates, including consistently altered graph fields. The coordinator independently reviews and refreshes the lock, regenerates current plan/brief/register bindings and runs normal and optimized-Python refusal controls. These checks establish static planning integrity only; RR16b/RR17 and independent review retain behavioral acceptance authority. This amendment grants no implementation or execution lease and records no new runtime result.
